(** The polymorphic face of division. Honoring `Frac` gives a type the `/`
    operator; the quotient is exact where the type is exact and rounded where
    it is not.

    The member below states the law an instance is reviewed against
    (`spec/constraints.md` section 7). `Rat` keeps it exactly; `Float` keeps it
    only up to rounding, failing outright at overflow, underflow, and `NaN`.
    The compiler relies on no such law: operands are evaluated in the rewritten
    form's source order, and no expression is rewritten by an algebraic law. *)
export constraint Frac<a: Signed> =
    (** `left` divided by `right`. For every nonzero `right`, `divide` is the
        right inverse of multiplying by `right`: `multiply(divide(left, right),
        right)` is `left`. An instance whose `multiply` is not commutative
        documents that its `divide` is not also a left inverse. *)
    divide(left: a, right: a): a
